Z||000000||Philphine||01-28-2001||11:47 AM||||<BR>just info gathering. wondering if anyone knows how much the stock seats weight. also for those who have the 1 piece race seats, is there any incovienience not being able to fold them forward? i keep a soft briefcase behind my seat to make up for not having a glove box. i'd need to get to it. and also if i try a behind the seat sub install. any info appreciated.<P>------------------<BR>Phil T<P>'87 coupe (feral)<BR>'84 indy<BR>'84 coupe (cheap thrill)<BR>'84 chop top (parts car or project. time will tell)||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||01-28-2001||03:42 PM||||I doubt you'll save much weight changing seats. The OE ones are mostly blocks of injection formed foam. They arean't very heavy. no I don't have exact weight.||||reg||1
Z||000002||danny boy||01-28-2001||05:55 PM||||I'm not sure about stock seat weight, but I have a pair of Coubeau Forza seats and they weigh 13lbs each. just lifting both, there is not a great deal of difference.<BR> You shouldnt have any problem with getting anything behind them,there is more room now then there was before,and mine slide forward enough to get stuff in/out easy.I used my stock seat brackets and some bar stock to mount them.||||reg||1
